From: Polaris Lab <polaris@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: pmi8998_fg: fix fallback current sign

pmi8998_fg_get_current() converts the PMIC current to the power supply
convention where charging is positive. The status fallback still treats
negative current as charging, reversing the displayed state when no
charger supply reference is available. Compare the converted current
using the same convention. Leave the exported current and charger
status path unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Polaris Lab <polaris@localhost>
---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
@@ -344,9 +344,10 @@
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
 				break;
 			}
-			if (temp < 0)
+			/* get_current() already converts to positive charging current. */
+			if (temp > 0)
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-			else if (temp > 0)
+			else if (temp < 0)
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 			else
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
